---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { factIssuerCount } from '../lib/facts.mjs';

const issuerCount = factIssuerCount();

const lastUpdated = '2026-11-11';
const siteOrigin = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL || 'https://defycard.com';
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: `${siteOrigin}/` },
  { name: 'Methodology', url: `${siteOrigin}/methodology/` },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology — how DefyCard verifies figures"
  description={`How DefyCard figures are verified: dated fact records for ${issuerCount} issuers, daily availability checks, and what the Verified badge and Last updated date mean.`}
  activeNav="cards"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <h1>Methodology</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      How a figure gets onto a DefyCard page, what the “Verified” badge and the
      “Last updated” date mean, and what we do not verify.
    </p>

    <h2>How a figure gets onto a page</h2>
    <p>
      Issuer facts are kept as dated records: each has a value, a source link,
      the date we verified it and an expiry date. We hold such records for
      {issuerCount} issuers. A record that is disputed or past its expiry is
      not rendered on any page.
    </p>
    <p>
      Draft text is produced with an AI model, not typed by hand. Before
      publication it passes automated gates, including one that refuses a money
      figure (a percentage, a dollar amount, a number of days) that matches none
      of our fact, rate or availability records. The editor named on the
      <a href="/editorial-policy/#editor">editorial policy</a> page owns the
      policy those gates implement.
    </p>

    <h2>Country availability</h2>
    <p>
      The country and US-state availability lists are compared with the
      issuer’s own list every day. Each list is published with the date it was
      last confirmed on the
      <a href="/geo/availability-matrix/">availability matrix</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What the labels mean</h2>
    <p>
      The “Verified” badge next to a figure prints the verification date and
      source link of the fact record behind that one figure; it says nothing
      about other numbers nearby. The “Last updated” date at the bottom of a
      page is the date of the latest edit of that page, not a re-verification
      of everything on it.
    </p>

    <h2>How lists are ordered</h2>
    <p>
      The order of cards in lists and comparisons is an editorial choice. No
      numeric score is assigned to any card.
    </p>

    <h2>What is not verified</h2>
    <p>
      Cards without a fact record carry dated figures only: the date printed
      next to a figure is the last time it was checked, and nothing promises a
      later re-check. The one list we re-check against the issuer on a daily
      schedule is availability by jurisdiction.
    </p>

    <p class="page-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .legal-page h2 {
    margin-top: 1.8em;
  }
  .legal-page p {
    color: var(--on-surface);
    margin: 0 0 1em;
  }
  .page-meta {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
  }
</style>
